## unreleased ##
    - rename module Type into Ty
    - the constructor and destructor arguments are named init and clear
      everywhere (Helper.abstract, custom, custom_ptr, on_stack, and Expert);
      Expert.mk_initialize and mk_finalize become mk_init and mk_clear
    - rename int_trunc into c_int, input_string/output_string into
      string_len/string_len_ref, input_array/output_array into
      array_len/array_len_ref (the old names are deprecated)
    - Expert.abstract takes expressions for icty and cty, like Expert.custom
    - add Helper.value_type for types handled like C++ classes (init,
      clear, copy), and Helper.extra_input
    - Helper.func ~error raises an exception (Failure or declared with
      Helper.exception_) when a C predicate on the result is true, after
      freeing the C values
    - Helper.func ~release_lock releases the runtime lock during the call;
      Ty.mlc.ml_heap marks the types that forbid it
    - identical C definitions with the same basename are printed once, so
      types can be built many times without duplicating code
    - add Ty.mlc.owned_by_ml; a parameter of such a type can't be input
      and output (it was finalized twice)
    - string_nt fails if the string contains a null byte, the previous
      behaviour is string_nt_prefix
    - remove the get, set, internal and malloc options of Helper.abstract,
      Helper.custom and Helper.custom_ptr (still in Expert)
    - fix leak of the elements of input_array and output_array
    - fix convert: the destination is initialized, the temporary is freed,
      the unboxed case is fixed
    - fix ignored_result: the result was not declared nor freed
    - fix bigarray_array1 conversion to C
    - documentation of the memory model

## 0.2 Second initial release ##
    - implement algdata as input
    - fix tests in release mode for ocaml < 5.2

## 0.1 Initial release ##

    - generic framework
    - helpers for common types
    - helpers for custom and abstract block
